1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In this tutorial you'll use the inspector to work with encoded values more easily.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,280
Open Burps browser and use it to access the following lab.

3
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:20,880
The lab is entitled Modifying Serialized Objects.

4
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:25,360
Click Access the lab and log in to your Portswigger account if prompted.

5
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:29,840
This opens your own instance of a deliberately vulnerable blog website.

6
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:35,640
Click My Account and log in using the credentials on the accompanying tutorial page.

7
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:40,160
These are Weiner and password Peter.

8
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:46,280
Go to the proxy HTTP tab and select the Get My Account Request.

9
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:52,800
In the inspector panel, expand the request cookies section.

10
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,840
Drill down on the recession cookie.

11
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,780
Click the arrow icon to the right.

12
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:02,980
Notice that the inspector automatically performs the correct sequence of decoding steps to

13
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,580
the value of the cookie.

14
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:13,660
In this case, it shows the result after URL decoding and then after the subsequent Base64 decoding.

15
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:19,580
Right click the Get My Account Request and select Send to Repeater.

16
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:24,380
Go to the Repeater tab and drill down into the Session Cookie again.

17
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:27,380
In Repeater, you can modify the decoded value.

18
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:34,380
For example, in the Decoded from Base64 field, change Weiner to Administrator.

19
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:37,380
Then click Apply Changes.

20
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:44,580
Notice that the inspector automatically re-applies the correct sequence of encodings when inserting the modified value into the request.

21
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:51,380
You can also select arbitrary strings in the message editor to examine them in the inspector.

22
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:57,380
Go back to the main inspector view, then highlight the value of the Session Cookie manually.

23
00:01:57,380 --> 00:02:02,380
Notice that the inspector automatically decodes your selection in the same way as before.

24
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:10,180
This is especially useful for working with substrings and non-standard data structures that the inspector is unable to parse automatically.

25
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:14,180
You've now learned how to use the inspector to work with encoded values more easily.

26
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:20,180
To learn more, refer to our online documentation or the Customizing the Inspector documentation page.

27
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:20,180


28
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,180
!

